This directory, interop/go/cometbft-crypto-merkle/ in the truestamp_merkle
repository, is a Go program that confirms the fixture file
vectors/interop/cometbft-crypto-merkle.json against
github.com/cometbft/cometbft/crypto/merkle, and can check the library's own
vectors/merkle.json with the same implementation. It contains third-party
material from the upstream module listed below.

Upstream: github.com/cometbft/cometbft
Version:  v1.0.1
License:  Apache-2.0. The license text is LICENSE-cometbft, a byte-for-byte
          copy of LICENSE at the root of github.com/cometbft/cometbft@v1.0.1.
          The module ships no NOTICE file, and its LICENSE names no copyright
          holder.
Material in this directory:
  upstream.go        test literals and test helpers copied from
                     crypto/merkle/rfc6962_test.go, crypto/merkle/tree_test.go,
                     crypto/merkle/proof_test.go, crypto/merkle/proof.go,
                     crypto/merkle/types.go, libs/test/mutate.go,
                     abci/types/types_test.go, types/block_test.go,
                     types/encoding_helper.go, types/utils.go,
                     types/validator_set_test.go,
                     types/consensus_breakage_test.go and types/tx_test.go
  upstream_extra.go  test literals and test bodies copied from
                     internal/blocksync/msgs_test.go, types/part_set_test.go,
                     types/results_test.go, state/store_test.go and
                     types/tx_test.go
  impl.go            code adapted from crypto/merkle/proof.go:79-114
                     (Proof.Verify) and crypto/merkle/tree.go:15-27
                     (hashFromByteSlices)
  main.go            assertion and corruption logic adapted from the upstream
                     tests named above, cited by file and line where used,
                     and the refusal texts of crypto/merkle/proof.go:215 and
                     220, quoted in a fixture note
  ours.go            the refusal texts of crypto/merkle/proof.go:208, 215 and
                     220, matched to tell which check refused a case
  The fixture file this program writes and confirms
  (vectors/interop/cometbft-crypto-merkle.json) holds values taken from those
  test literals or produced by the upstream module's own functions.
